  "result": {
    "summary": "Commit 65559e3 (the T-1352 landing) is an empty commit. The T-1347 change is already in the base as b56150d, and `git diff 3925705 b56150d` is empty, so it is the same code. I read the b56150d hunks in pool.py and daemon.py. `executor_identity` resolves from cfg only, with no disk read. Claude executor rows require account headroom in `eligible_executors`, and `pick` is called at most once and only when a Claude row exists. `codex_available` is now Codex-only. Review tier selection goes through `_model_review_tier`, which fails closed to the other tier on any lookup error. `_open_reviews` loads config at most once and passes `pool.cfg` from the gate and lease-sweep callers. All 11 named acceptance tests are present as TestCase methods in tests/test_pool.py and tests/test_daemon.py, and the daemon gate recorded one attempt with no reds. I did not re-run the suite. No trust-boundary or privilege issues found.",
    "verdict": "approve",
